                0.888
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 11.9: (a) A light beam (b) Reflection of light in a plane mirror"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.006,
                0.895,
                0.285,
                0.958
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_12.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.488,
            0.856,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take a plane mirror with stand, a torch, a comb, a sheet of white paper, and a strip of black paper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.387,
            0.529,
            0.856,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using the black paper, close all openings of the comb, except for one to make a thin slit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.57,
            0.857,
            0.68
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Spread a white paper on a table, hold the comb perpendicular to the sheet of paper and shine the torch light on the slit. Adjust the comb and torch slightly till you see a thin beam of light along the paper which has passed through the slit (Fig. 11.9a)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.388,
            0.684,
            0.857,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, place the mirror in the path of the light beam while keeping the comb steady (Fig. 11.9b). What do you observe?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.046,
            0.901,
            0.088,
            0.919
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "160"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.387,
            0.743,
            0.856,
            0.797
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The path of the light beam is changed after falling on the mirror. The reflection of light occurs at the mirror."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.428,
            0.815,
            0.676,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In a mirror, I can also see my face. Is that also due to the reflection of light?"
            }
          ]
        },
